  "The phrase “less is more” was actually first popularized by a German, the architect Ludwig Mies van der Rohe, who like other people associated with the Bauhaus, a school of design, emigrated to the United States before World War II and took up posts at American architecture schools.": "“少即是多”这句话实际上最早由德国建筑师路德维希·密斯·凡德罗推广开来，他与包豪斯设计学院的其他相关人员一样，在二战前移民到美国，并在美国建筑学院任职。",
  "On July 29th they were relieved, at least temporarily.": "7月29日，他们松了一口气，至少暂时如此。",
