  "Many Americans regard the jury system as a concrete expression of crucial democratic values, including the principles that all citizens who meet minimal qualifications of age and literacy are equally competent to serve on juries; that jurors should be selected randomly from a representative cross section of the community; that no citizen should be denied the right to serve on a jury on account of race, religion, sex, or national origin; that defendants are entitled to trial by their peers; and that verdicts should represent the conscience of the community and not just the letter of the law.": "许多美国人将陪审团制度视为关键民主价值观的具体体现，这些价值观包括：所有达到最低年龄和识字资格的公民都同样有资格担任陪审员；陪审员应从具有代表性的社区横截面中随机挑选；任何公民都不应因种族、宗教、性别或民族血统而被剥夺担任陪审员的权利；被告有权由同龄人审判；以及裁决应代表社区的良知，而不仅仅是法律条文。",
  "\"We'd assumed we'd have to give it a moving head and tail, facial features, and put a scent on it to make it smell like a real rat, but that wasn't necessary,\" says Janet Wiles at the University of Queensland in Australia, who helped with the research.": "澳大利亚昆士兰大学的珍妮特·威尔士参与了这项研究，她说：“我们原本以为必须给它装上会动的头和尾巴、面部特征，还要喷上气味让它闻起来像真的老鼠，但事实证明这并不必要。”",
  "Newspapers are becoming more balanced businesses, with a healthier mix of revenues from readers and advertisers.": "报纸正成为更加平衡的行业，来自读者和广告商的收入结构更加健康。",
