  "Primary care providers have their hands full and may not be able to follow through with patients who have trouble driving because they can't turn their heads or remember where they are going—or have gotten shorter and haven't changed their seat settings sufficiently to reach car pedals easily.": "初级保健提供者已经忙得不可开交，可能无法跟进那些开车有困难的患者，因为他们无法转头或记不住要去哪里——或者个子变矮了，却没有充分调整座椅设置以便轻松踩到踏板。",
  "This time experts reckon that prices are about 40% down on their peak on average, though some have been far more fluctuant.": "这次专家们估计，价格平均比峰值下降了约40%，尽管有些价格波动更为剧烈。",
  "Programming languages have a quick turnover, so the \\\\\"Ruby on Rails\\\\\" language they learned may not even be relevant by the time they enter the job market.": "编程语言更迭迅速，因此他们学到的“Ruby on Rails”语言，到他们进入就业市场时可能已经过时了。",
  "Koziatek is part of something pioneering.": "科齐亚特克参与了一项开创性的事业。",
  "The climate change we are hastening could one day leave us with forests that emit more carbon than they absorb.": "我们正在加速的气候变化，有朝一日可能使森林排放的碳超过其吸收的量。",
  "This law abolished special educational requirements for federal jurors and required them to be selected at random from a cross section of the entire community.": "这项法律废除了对联邦陪审员的特殊教育要求，并要求从整个社区的各个阶层中随机挑选陪审员。",
  "It's not hard to imagine a similar reversal happening in London.": "不难想象伦敦也会发生类似的逆转。",
