  "This slim volume is packed with tips to help wage slaves as well as lottery winners get the most \"happiness bang for your buck.\" It seems most people would be better off if they could shorten their commutes to work, spend more time with friends and family and less of it watching television (something the average American spends a whopping two months a year doing, and is hardly jollier for it).": "这本薄薄的书里满是建议，帮助工薪族和彩票中奖者从花出的每一分钱中获得最大的“幸福回报”。看来，如果大多数人能缩短通勤时间，花更多时间与朋友和家人在一起，少看电视（普通美国人平均每年花整整两个月看电视，却并未因此更快乐），他们的生活可能会更好。",
  "But one specific complaint is made especially mournfully: There's never any time to read.": "但有一个具体的抱怨尤为哀怨：从来都没有时间读书。",
