  "The survey then asks whether they worked less than 35 hours in that week because they wanted to work less than full time or because they had no choice.": "调查随后询问他们那一周工作时间是否少于35小时，是因为他们想少于全职时间工作，还是因为别无选择。",
  "To ensure that all employees were paid fair wages, some restaurants banned tipping and increased prices, but this movement toward no-tipping services has largely fizzled out.": "为了确保所有员工获得公平的工资，一些餐馆禁止小费并提高价格，但这种无小费服务的运动在很大程度上已经不了了之。",
  "As demand for healthcare continues to grow, pressures on the workforce—which is already near breaking point—will only become more acute.": "随着医疗保健需求的持续增长，本已接近崩溃边缘的劳动力所面临的压力只会变得更加严峻。",
  "It's just that individual actions are too slow, she says, for that to be the only, or even primary, approach to changing widespread behavior.": "她说，问题在于个人行动太缓慢，无法成为改变广泛行为的唯一甚至主要途径。",
